% INVALID certificate: min x, x in [0,10] integer, has optimum 0, but the lower bound 1 is "proved" by refuting the
% cutoff OBJ <= -1, which relies on a best solution value of 0 although the SOL section is empty.
VER 1.1
VAR 1
x
INT 1
0
OBJ min
1 0 1
CON 2 0
C1 G 0 1 0 1
C2 L 10 1 0 1
RTP range 1 inf
SOL 0
DER 3
D1 L -1 OBJ { sol } -1
D2 G 1 0 { lin 2 0 1 2 -1 } -1
D3 G 1 OBJ { lin 1 3 1 } -1
